-- title:
--   Membership in a base-changed Hilbert point via graded pieces
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $n$, a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$, commutative rings $B$ and $A$, and a ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to A$. Let $P$ be a point of the Hilbert functor over $B$ and $Q$ one over $A$ for the same $h$; that is, each consists of an ideal of the polynomial ring in $n+1$ variables over the respective base which is stable under taking homogeneous components, together with the data that for every $d$ the $d$-th graded piece — the degree-$d$ homogeneous submodule modulo its intersection with the ideal — is a finite projective module whose rank at every prime of the base is $h(d)$. Assume the base-change relation $Q.I = \varphi(P.I)\,A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$, i.e. $Q.I$ is the ideal generated by the image of $P.I$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\varphi$. Let $d$ be a natural number and let $F$ be a polynomial over $B$ in $n+1$ variables that is homogeneous of degree $d$. Then $\varphi(F)$, the image of $F$ under the coefficientwise map, lies in $Q.I$ if and only if, regarding $A$ as a $B$-algebra via $\varphi$, the element $1 \otimes [F]$ of $A \otimes_B \mathrm{piece}(P.I, d)$ vanishes, where $[F]$ denotes the class of $F$ in the $d$-th graded piece of $P.I$.
--
--   This is the base-change criterion for membership in a Hilbert point: it converts the condition that the base-changed ideal contains $\varphi(F)$ into the vanishing of a single element of the base change of a finite projective module. It is used in the proof of the characterisation of points of the Hilbert functor admitting a closed immersion of finite presentation through which given homogeneous forms factor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_HilbertFunctor_map_mem_iff_tmul_mkQ_piece_eq_zero.lean

